.TH "CASCADE-TSIG" "1" "Jan 01, 2026" "0.1.0-beta7-dev" "Cascade"
.SH NAME
cascade-tsig \- Manage TSIG keys
.sp
Added in version 0.1.0\-beta1.

.SH SYNOPSIS
.sp
\fBcascade\fP \fB[GLOBAL OPTIONS]\fP tsig \fB<COMMAND>\fP
.sp
\fBcascade\fP \fB[GLOBAL OPTIONS]\fP tsig \fI\%add\fP \fB<PATH>\fP
.sp
\fBcascade\fP \fB[GLOBAL OPTIONS]\fP tsig \fI\%list\fP
.sp
\fBcascade\fP \fB[GLOBAL OPTIONS]\fP tsig \fI\%remove\fP \fB<TSIG_KEY_NAME>\fP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.sp
Manage \X'tty: link https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8945.html'\fI\%RFC 8945\fP\X'tty: link' (TSIG) keys for authenticating zone transfer (AXFR, IXFR) and
related messages (SOA and NOTIFY).
.sp
\fBTIP:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Cascade isn\(aqt currently able to generate TSIG keys itself.
One way to generate a TSIG key is to use the \X'tty: link https://bind9.readthedocs.io/en/latest/manpages.html#tsig-keygen-tsig-key-generation-tool'\fI\%tsig\-keygen\fP\X'tty: link' tool from the ISC BIND project.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.sp
See \fI\%Cascade CLI\fP for information about global options supported by every CLI
command.
.SH COMMANDS
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B add
Add a new TSIG key.
.sp
Incoming DNS messages that are TSIG signed will be rejected if the key used
to sign the message is not registered with Cascade.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B list
List registered TSIG keys.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B remove
Remove a TSIG key.
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 7.0
.INDENT 3.5
Returns an error if the key does not exist in the TSIG key store,
or if the key is still referenced by other configuration.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SH ARGUMENTS FOR TSIG ADD
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B <PATH>
Path to the file containing the TSIG key.
.sp
The file format is specified by \fB\-\-format\fP\&.
.sp
Regardless of the file format the file must contain all the following
values exactly once.
.sp
The name of the key to add, TSIG key names must be valid domain names.
.sp
The algorithm of the specified TSIG key. Can be one of: \fBhmac\-sha1\fP,
\fBhmac\-sha256\fP, \fBhmac\-sha384\fP or \fBhmac\-sha512\fP\&.
.sp
The secret key material must be the correct length for the specified algorithm
and must be encoded using the \X'tty: link https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc4648.html'\fI\%RFC 4648\fP\X'tty: link' Base64 encoding.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-format <FORMAT>
Format used in the TSIG file.
.sp
The \fBNSD\fP and \fBKnot\fP formats are not parsed with full YAML compliance.
.sp
Possible values:
.INDENT 7.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBnsd\fP:  \X'tty: link https://nsd.docs.nlnetlabs.nl/en/latest/running/using-tsig.html'\fI\%NSD TSIG Documentation\fP\X'tty: link'
.IP \(bu 2
\fBbind\fP: \X'tty: link https://bind9.readthedocs.io/en/stable/reference.html#namedconf-statement-key'\fI\%BIND TSIG Documentation\fP\X'tty: link'
.IP \(bu 2
\fBknot\fP: \X'tty: link https://www.knot-dns.cz/docs/latest/html/reference.html#key-section'\fI\%Knot TSIG Documentation\fP\X'tty: link'
.UNINDENT
.sp
[default: nsd]
.UNINDENT
